 example \n Week 5: projected lineup #2 among 4 fictional teams with comparable lineups. This compares projections, not league standings. Eligible backups:  Jalen Hurts (QB): 24 projected points; DeVonta Smith (WR): 7 projected points; Ja\'Marr Chase (WR): 8 projected points; George Kittle (TE): 4 projected points Keep in mind:  Using a reserve quarterback to improve receivers can remove that quarterback cover. Current points do not establish future availability. Consider next:  Compare a receiver upgrade with its quarterback-depth cost before pursuing it. \n Starting lineup and useful replacements Fictional week 5 projections under this example\'s rules. Bench players are not counted in the starting total. Starting lineup QB Josh Allen Starting slot: QB 34 pts QB Lamar Jackson Starting slot: SUPER_FLEX 30 pts RB Bijan Robinson Starting slot: FLEX 16 pts TE Brock Bowers Starting slot: TE 10 pts WR CeeDee Lamb Starting slot: WR 10 pts RB Christian McCaffrey Starting slot: RB 8 pts Available replacements QB Jalen Hurts 24 pts WR DeVonta Smith 7 pts WR Ja\'Marr Chase 8 pts TE George Kittle 4 pts \n Exact draft capital 2028 first · originally Summit Front Office Original franchise: Summit Front Office · Current owner: Harbor Front Office Original franchise and current ownership remain separate. A pick is not guaranteed to be early or to produce a particular player. \n \n 02 Make Better Trades \n Illustrative values and hypothetical rosters. Not live player valuations or actual trades. Hypothetical offer · Harbor Front Office and Summit Front Office \n You Send QB Lamar Jackson You Receive WR Justin Jefferson 528 You send · neutral Market units 528 You receive · neutral Market units WORTH PURSUING Eligible in this fictional evaluation. An evaluated hypothetical offer, not a prediction that another manager accepts. Both rosters are evaluated using the same neutral evidence. \n Harbor Front Office +12 projected points  · strongest legal lineup 108 → 120 Benefit:  The incom